From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0145: blueline: zero-copy present, DPU scans out
 backboardd's surface (bluedpu_flip=1)

On top of 0140 v2. AppleCLCD::swap only recorded the frame and the vsync
timer copied (and scaled) it into ABL's panel buffer at sweetfb_hz
(default 10 Hz); SwapWait is a no-op and no swap-complete is sent.

bluedpu_flip=1 (default 0): a swap of exactly one enabled layer showing a
whole 1125x2436 BGRA surface at the origin points the staged SSPPs
(VIG0 -> LM0, VIG1 -> LM1) at that surface:
- only surfaces from a scanout pool: bluedpu_flip_bufs (default 3, 2..4)
  contiguous buffers below 4 GiB (SSPP addresses are 32-bit; the MDP
  streams are untranslated), allocated at AppleCLCD::start and never
  freed; SweetSurface hands them to backboardd's display-sized BGRA
  surfaces. Contiguity and the 4 GiB limit are checked again per flip.
- geometry follows bluefb_fit: QSEED3 fit (default; each LM half scales
  its source columns, 1125x2436 -> 997x2160 at x 41, bilinear, pixel
  extension = source size, bars = LM border colour) or the centre crop
  (bluefb_fit=0, same as the bluedpu=2 test).
- clean to PoC, write (geometry on the first flip, then only the
  addresses), CTL_FLUSH of the pipe bits, wait (IOSleep(1), 50 ms bound)
  until the bits clear = the frame start that took it. SwapEnd returns
  after that, so the swap is complete when backboardd gets control back.
- everything else (more layers, other sizes, the console surface,
  display off, a pending flush) is copied as before; the timer points the
  pipes back at the panel buffer after copying. Each reason is logged
  once.
- display off (0123): the panel buffer is blacked and the pipes go back
  to it before the fade; no flips while off. Panic (PEInitiatePanic, no
  locks, no wait) and halt/restart (PEHaltRestart) restore ABL's
  registers so the panic screen and console are visible.
- a flush that does not latch, a new INTF underrun, an SMMU fault-state
  change on the MDP streams' bank or no pp_done for a second (checked
  every 60 vsync ticks) turns the flip off for the boot.

bluedpu=3: the bluedpu=2 test with the fit geometry (whole test buffer
framed in magenta), to check QSEED3 before iOS uses it.

bluedpu_stats: every 5 s also flips, unflips, clean and latch time.
